(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108 aliasing probe: `a text called b is orig.` copies
 orig's POINTER, not its bytes (Set t to src is the same shape the bug
 report measured flat) - two names for one string. `orig` is therefore
 read in a retaining position and must never be freed on its own `Set`,
 or `b` would be left pointing at freed memory. Before and after the fix
 this must print "5" - freeing here would be a use-after-free, worse than
 the leak #108 exists to close.)

a number called n is 5.
a text called orig is "{n}".
a text called b is orig.
Set orig to "{n}".
Print b.
